  "text": {
   "approach": "Reached only by first climbing Mount Crowder by its Southwest Route, from the col between Phantom Peak and Crowder, and continuing down the far side; there is no separate trailhead approach to this ridge on its own.",
   "approach_logistics": "{\"peakLat\":48.7976266,\"peakLng\":-121.352631,\"trailhead\":\"No separate trailhead — over Mount Crowder by its Southwest Route\"}",
   "road": "{\"name\":\"Ruth Creek Rd / Hannegan Pass Rd (FR-32)\",\"status\":\"Seasonal USFS road, subject to washout\",\"driveNote\":\"From WA-542 (Mt. Baker Hwy), follow FR-32 about 5.3 mi to road's end at the Hannegan Pass Trailhead; recent storm damage has at times restricted vehicles to around mile 5.2 — check current Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie NF alerts before you go.\",\"seasonalGate\":\"Typically opens once snow clears in early-mid summer and closes with the first significant fall snow.\"}",
   "overview": "A direct, technical ridge line dropping northeast off Crowder's summit toward Pickell Pass. It is documented as a descent used by parties continuing a Pickets high-route traverse northward, not as a recommended way to reach Crowder's summit, and is significantly harder and more hazardous than the Southwest Route.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": "From the summit, the ridge is down-climbed via a mix of loose, grassy Class 3-4 ledges with occasional low-5th-class moves, working around a large chasm partway down, and negotiating a final cliff band (found via a scree-slope break) before reaching Pickell Pass."
  },
